{"step_index":366,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-08T22:01:16Z","input_tokens":3035,"cache_read_tokens":239241,"output_tokens":1642,"thinking":"Initial observation: `defaultQuiz` is also embedded in `teacher.html`. The goal is to remove the default quiz loading. Removing `defaultQuiz` from `teacher.html` will cause the page to load `quizzes/active` from Firestore directly. If `quizzes/active` exists in Firestore, `teacher.html` will load from Firestore; otherwise, it will show an empty question.\n\n\nThe Firebase rules now permit direct writes to the `quizzes/{quizId}` document from `teacher.html`, resolving the permission error. Saving quiz data will write directly to Firestore, confirming the quiz is live. The ability to upload `index.html` as `quizzes/template` in Firestore allows immediate access and download.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":true,\"Summary\":\"Implementation plan to replace the quiz download button in teacher.html with a 'Download QUIZ Json' button that downloads index.html (retrievable from Firestore template or local source), remove defaultQuiz from firebase-config.js, and align with the user's updated Firestore rules (allow read, write: if true on quizzes).\",\"UserFacing\":true}","Content":"\"# Implementation Plan: Download Student Quiz HTML, Remove defaultQuiz, & Align with Updated Rules\\n\\n## 1. Overview of Requested Changes\\n1. **Remove `defaultQuiz` from [firebase-config.js](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/firebase-config.js)**:\\n   - Purge the static `defaultQuiz` definition and 20 hardcoded switch-case questions from `firebase-config.js`.\\n2. **Download Student Quiz (`index.html`) from [teacher.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/teacher.html)**:\\n   - Replace the previous JSON export button with a **`Download QUIZ Json`** button.\\n   - When clicked, this button generates and downloads the complete stan